WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.998 --> 00:00:12.566
Five hundred years ago, a woman of extraordinary abilities earned respect for her talent as a painter and

2
00:00:12.606 --> 00:00:19.932
poet. She lived in the tradition-bound society of ancient Korea, and her family cherished her as a devoted

3
00:00:19.993 --> 00:00:21.534
daughter, mother, and wife.

4
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:28.500
Today, we recognize her as a woman who pioneered independence and individuality for women.

5
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:37.325
Shin Saim-dang was born in Korea in 1504 during the Chosun Dynasty.

6
00:00:38.226 --> 00:00:41.869
The second of five daughters, she was named In-sun at birth.

7
00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:48.314
At a young age, she chose the pen name Saim-dang, which means "loving mother of the king."

8
00:00:49.135 --> 00:00:54.780
Her inspiration was the mother of King Wen, a ruler in the Zhou Dynasty of ancient China.

9
00:00:57.308 --> 00:01:04.590
During the Chosun Dynasty, most Koreans abided by Confucian teachings, which held that a son must look after

10
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:05.250
his parents.

11
00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:11.552
For this reason, after a man was married, his wife would leave her family to go and live

12
00:01:11.592 --> 00:01:12.833
with her husband's family.

13
00:01:15.353 --> 00:01:20.815
Although Saim-dang's family honored Confucian teachings, they did not always follow tradition.

14
00:01:21.795 --> 00:01:28.195
Saim-dang's mother was an only child, so Saim-dang's grandparents had no son to take care of them.

15
00:01:29.116 --> 00:01:35.280
With the consent of her husband, Saim-dang's mother continued to live at home even after she married.

16
00:01:36.461 --> 00:01:42.945
Thus, Saim-dang was born in her mother's childhood home, called Ojukheon, in the city of Gangneung.

17
00:01:44.807 --> 00:01:51.712
Saim-dang's father worked in Seoul, 150 kilometers away, so she did not see him very often.

18
00:01:52.756 --> 00:01:57.699
Her mother and grandfather took on the responsibility of raising her and her sisters.

19
00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:04.344
The five girls all learned to read and write, even though most girls at the time received little

20
00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:12.309
education. In this atmosphere of learning, Saim-dang developed an appreciation for the arts.

21
00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.852
She enjoyed practicing calligraphy and composing poetry.

22
00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:23.631
At the age of seven, she studied the works of Ahn Gyeun, a famous painter who lived during

23
00:02:23.731 --> 00:02:26.792
King Sejong's rule, one hundred years earlier.

24
00:02:27.872 --> 00:02:32.895
Saim-dang imitated Ahn Gyeun's brushstrokes as she developed her own style of painting.

25
00:02:34.595 --> 00:02:41.478
Her favorite subjects were the things she saw every day in the backyard of Ojukheon: flowers, clusters of

26
00:02:41.538 --> 00:02:44.760
grapes, bamboo trees, butterflies, and insects.

27
00:02:45.992 --> 00:02:50.695
It is said that Saim-dang's drawings were so lifelike they deceived even animals.

28
00:02:52.096 --> 00:02:57.399
One summer day, after completing a painting with an ant in it, she set it aside to dry.

29
00:02:57.419 --> 00:03:02.021
"I'll just go inside to get a drink," she said to herself.

30
00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:08.345
A chicken in the garden saw the painting and, thinking that the ant was real, started to peck

31
00:03:08.425 --> 00:03:09.326
at it with its beak.

32
00:03:09.986 --> 00:03:13.736
When Saim-dang saw what the chicken was doing, she cried, "No!

33
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:14.617
Stop that!

34
00:03:14.857 --> 00:03:15.918
It's not real!"

35
00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:18.180
But it was too late.

36
00:03:19.181 --> 00:03:20.862
Her painting was torn to pieces.

37
00:03:24.385 --> 00:03:30.090
At the age of 19, Saim-dang married a man who lived in Seoul, but only a few months

38
00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.652
after the wedding, her father passed away.

39
00:03:33.593 --> 00:03:38.517
Having no brothers, Saim-dang felt it was her duty to take care of her widowed mother.

40
00:03:39.638 --> 00:03:44.546
Her new husband was a caring man, and he allowed her to return to Ojukheon.

41
00:03:47.268 --> 00:03:52.532
In those days, it was customary for families to mourn their dead loved ones for three years.

42
00:03:53.573 --> 00:03:55.894
Saim-dang spent this period with her mother.

43
00:03:56.855 --> 00:03:59.577
Then she traveled back to Seoul to be with her husband.

44
00:04:00.558 --> 00:04:02.960
Her eldest child, a son, was born there.

45
00:04:04.101 --> 00:04:08.264
As much as she was a faithful daughter, Saim-dang was also a devoted wife.

46
00:04:09.928 --> 00:04:14.549
She diligently performed the duties set for her by Confucian tradition in her husband's home.

47
00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:17.950
"Is the rice warm enough, Mother-in-law?"

48
00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.831
she would ask at mealtimes.

49
00:04:21.091 --> 00:04:26.712
She treated her husband's family with the utmost respect, but she was also kind to those who helped

50
00:04:26.773 --> 00:04:27.453
around the house.

51
00:04:27.473 --> 00:04:31.554
"Thank you," she would say with a smile to servants.

52
00:04:40.332 --> 00:04:42.453
Heartbroken that her mother was alone, Saim-dang often returned to Ojukheon.

53
00:04:42.473 --> 00:04:45.956
In 1536, during one of her stays there, she gave birth to her fifth child.

54
00:04:47.016 --> 00:04:53.321
She named him Yi Yi, and he spent his childhood in Ojukheon, cared for by his mother and

55
00:04:53.341 --> 00:05:01.926
grandmother. Yi Yi learned Chinese script at the age of three and composed poems before he reached his

56
00:05:01.986 --> 00:05:02.847
seventh birthday.

57
00:05:03.828 --> 00:05:07.490
He grew up to become one of Korea's greatest Confucian scholars.

58
00:05:08.551 --> 00:05:10.252
Saim-dang had seven children.

59
00:05:11.196 --> 00:05:16.440
Just as her parents had instilled a thirst for knowledge in her, she taught all her children the

60
00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:17.561
importance of learning.

61
00:05:20.003 --> 00:05:25.888
Despite her busy days looking after her mother and her own family, Saim- dang always found time to

62
00:05:25.948 --> 00:05:27.269
pursue her love of the arts.

63
00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:33.133
As much as she upheld traditions, she was also not afraid to express how she felt.

64
00:05:34.054 --> 00:05:36.236
Her reputation as an artist and poet grew.

65
00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:43.321
"Her strokes are bold yet feminine," one person remarked.

66
00:05:44.401 --> 00:05:47.342
"It's elegant and beautiful," commented another.

67
00:05:48.623 --> 00:05:53.664
Despite her popularity, Saim-dang was humble and did not draw attention to herself.

68
00:05:54.684 --> 00:05:58.225
Her passion in life was art, but her love was for her family.

69
00:05:59.406 --> 00:06:03.907
In his writings, Yi Yi credits his success to his mother's loving upbringing.

70
00:06:04.827 --> 00:06:11.121
Living in a time when a woman's role was limited, Shin Saim-dang proved that women had the ability

71
00:06:11.241 --> 00:06:14.486
and talents to contribute greatly to art and learning.

72
00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.851
She was truly a woman before her time.
